was whoever the scheduler let in.\n\nReproduced pre-fix: **10/40 focused runs failed** (~25%), 1009 beating 1007.\n\n## Fix\n\nCapture ordering where the caller still exists instead of where the work runs. New file-private `ProviderFailureAdmission` (`NSLock`-guarded claim) in `Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/ProviderLifecycle.swift:461`; `providerDidFail` claims it **synchronously** before spawning the task (`:907`), so later/concurrent callers are dropped before reaching the actor. `startGeneration` releases the claim on generation bump (`:632`), keeping the same per-generation scoping the old ledger had.\n\nRemoved `cancelTunnelIssuedGeneration` — with synchronous admission it's unreachable, and two exactly-once authorities on one callback would drift apart eventually. Diff is +26/−6 in one source file; stop/join semantics, NSError codes, and cleanup-registry behavior untouched. Both seams inherit it (the roots forward straight through at `:146`).\n\n## Coverage and gates\n\nThree new tests, both seams:\n- `providerFailureFirstCallOrdering` — 50 double-failure cycles. **Verified it actually catches the bug**: with the source fix stashed it fails on both seams; with it, green.\n- `providerFailureConcurrentAdmission` — 16 concurrent calls, each cancel handler reentrantly re-calling `providerDidFail`. This is what protects the `cancelTunnelIssuedGeneration` removal (it passed pre-fix too, by design).\n- `providerFailureAdmissionResetsPerGeneration` — guards against the claim latching forever.\n\n| Gate | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `providerFailureHandoff` × 30 | **0/30 failures** |\n| `swift test` | **exit 0**, 335 tests / 29 suites |\n| `make validate-core` | **exit 0** |\n| `make check-core-boundaries` | exit 0 |\n| `swift-format lint --strict` | exit 0 |\n\nEvidence on the board as `BUG-260728-3jfjkh_results.md`; logs in `.temp/BUG-260728-3jfjkh/`; logbook entry added.\n\nTwo things worth flagging, ахпер:\n- AC5's \"independently reviewed\" is the reviewer's step, not mine — that's the one criterion I can't self-certify.\n- Repo has no root `.swift-format` config (only `Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH/` has one), so I linted with swift-format defaults. Nothing to fix, but the root package's lint gate is effectively just `check-core-boundaries` right now.\n\nNothing staged or committed.","ttft_ms":5224,"ttft_stream_ms":4755,"time_to_request_ms":19,"type":"result","duration_ms":516948,"uuid":"29423393-cd9b-4e68-b9a5-217378dc9417"}
